<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n86189" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρᾰπίδες</span></b> , αἱ, dat.
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πραπίσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					2.94
				</span></i>
			, 
				Ep.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πραπίδεσσι</span> (v. infr.):—
			poet., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρένες</span>
			, <i>midriff, diaphragm,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάλε . . ἦπαρ ὑπὸ πραπίδων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					11.579
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				13.412
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				17.349
			</span></i>: then, since this was deemed the seat of mental powers and
			affections, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>understanding, mind,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰδυίῃσι πραπίδεσσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.608
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				18.380
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ μὲν πραπίδες, περὶ δ᾽ ἐστὶ νόημα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					656
				</span></i>
			; as the seat of desire, <i>heart,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ πραπίδων ἦλθ᾽ ἵμερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					24.514
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔσχεν ἄκοιτιν ἀρηρυῖαν
				πραπίδεσσιν</span> wins a wife after his own <i>heart,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				608
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάσῃσιν ὀρέξαιτο πραπίδεσσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					129.4
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πραπίδων πλοῦτος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				11(10).10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>P.</u>
				4.281
			</span></i>; Trag. in lyr., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὖ πραπίδων λαχόντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					380
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				802
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				480
			</span></i>: rarely in sg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πραπίς,</span>
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				2.61
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				109
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				427
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				999
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔργον ἐμῆς π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					14.1500
				</span></i>
			.</div>
